92186045417] [17592186083691 #edb/ref 1071 "$7.8\\overset{―}{7}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083691 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d2e6148-1311-589a-937a-5889bc0f6bfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083691 #edb/ref 1074 "The given repeating decimal can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.8\\overset{―}{7} & =7.877\\,7... \\\\  & =7.8+0.07+0.007+0.000\\,7+… \\\\  & =7.8+(\\frac{7}{100}+\\frac{7}{1\\,000}+\\frac{7}{10\\,000}+…).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series in the parentheses is a geometric series with first term ${a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{100}$ and common ratio $r=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.8\\overset{―}{7} & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{100}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7\\cdot 10}{100}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n} \\\\  & =7.8+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{10}{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084209 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084209 #edb/ref 1061 2380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084209 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d0db37f3-c116-58a6-a33d-41ca478ae931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084209 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084210 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084210 #edb/ref 1061 2381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084210 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "af145878-806f-54bc-991b-28bc9b80cc8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084210 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084211 #edb/ref 1061 2385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084211 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4af12d7e-248c-5555-bd4c-98e9849f98a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084211 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084397 #edb/ref 1064 "A repeating decimal can be expressed as a geometric series whose common ratio is a power of $\\dfrac 1 {10}.$\n\nFor example, the